{"builder":"Make one pull request that meets every acceptance line of issue https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7 (padLeft() for invoice numbers).\n\nThe repository is a small ES-module package: index.js exports capitalize, slugify and truncate; README.md documents them under `## name(args)` headings; test/strutil.test.js runs under `npm test` (`node --test`).\n\nSteps:\n1. In index.js, add and export `padLeft(s, width, fill)`, with a one-line doc comment like the other functions. It pads `s` on the left with `fill` until the result is `width` characters long. When `fill` is not given, it pads with a space. Examples: padLeft('42', 5, '0') === '00042' and padLeft('ab', 4) === '  ab'. `String.prototype.padStart` does this: `s.padStart(width, fill ?? ' ')`.\n2. padLeft must return `s` unchanged when `s.length >= width`. Examples: padLeft('abcde', 5, '0') === 'abcde' and padLeft('abcdef', 3) === 'abcdef'.\n3. README.md must have a section for every function index.js exports. Right now slugify has no section, so add one. Add `## slugify(s)`: it returns `s` trimmed, in lower case, with each run of non-alphanumeric characters replaced by a single dash and leading and trailing dashes removed. Also add `## padLeft(s, width, fill)`, saying what it pads with, that the default fill is a space, that `s` comes back unchanged when it is already `width` characters or longer, and giving the invoice example 42 -> 00042. Use the same heading style as the existing sections and keep the existing sections.\n4. In test/strutil.test.js, add padLeft tests: one with a fill, one with the default space fill, one where s is exactly width long and one where it is longer.\n5. Run `npm test` and make sure it passes. Then check that every function index.js exports has a README.md heading, for example with `node -e \"import('./index.js').then(m=>console.log(Object.keys(m)))\"`.\n6. Open the pull request and reference the issue.","verifier":"Check the pull request's head checkout for issue https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7. There is one check per acceptance line, in order. Run each command from the repository root. Report PASS or FAIL for each check and include the output you saw.\n\nCheck 1. Expect line: \"index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\"\nRun: `node --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; console.log(typeof m.padLeft, JSON.stringify(m.padLeft('42',5,'0')), JSON.stringify(m.padLeft('ab',4)), JSON.stringify(m.padLeft('7',3,'x')))\"`\nPASS: the output is `function \"00042\" \"  ab\" \"xx7\"`. That means padLeft is exported, pads on the left with the given fill, uses a space when no fill is given, and the result is width characters long.\nFAIL: padLeft is not exported or is not a function, the import throws, or any of the three results is different.\n\nCheck 2. Expect line: \"padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\"\nRun: `node --input-type=module -e \"import {padLeft} from './index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify(padLeft('abcde',5,'0')), JSON.stringify(padLeft('abcdef',3)), JSON.stringify(padLeft('abcdef',3,'0')))\"`\nPASS: the output is `\"abcde\" \"abcdef\" \"abcdef\"`. Both the equal-length input and the longer input come back unchanged.\nFAIL: any result differs from its input (padded, cut or otherwise changed), or the call throws.\n\nCheck 3. Expect line: \"README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\"\nRun: `node --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; console.log(Object.keys(m).filter(k=>typeof m[k]==='function').join(' '))\"` to list the exported functions at the head. Then read README.md at the head, or run `grep -n '^#' README.md`.\nPASS: every function in the list (at least capitalize, slugify, truncate and padLeft) has its own section in README.md, meaning a heading that names the function, with text under it describing it.\nFAIL: any exported function has no README.md section. Note that the base README has no slugify section, so a PR that adds only padLeft fails this check.\n\nCheck 4. Expect line: \"npm test passes\"\nRun: `npm test`.\nPASS: the run finishes with no failing tests and npm reports success.\nFAIL: any test fails, or the command errors.\n\nAdvisory (not part of PASS or FAIL):\n- Check whether the PR adds padLeft tests to test/strutil.test.js.\n- See how padLeft handles a multi-character fill, for example padLeft('1', 4, 'ab'). padStart returns 'aba1'.\n- Check whether the README headings follow the existing `## name(args)` style and whether the padLeft section mentions the default space fill."}